# Do not convert line endings on checkout or commit.
#
# 913 tracked files in this repo are CRLF, including 29 of the 30 Python modules
# under nextseek_api/batch_upload/. That is the historical norm here, not damage.
#
# `-text` tells git to store and check out bytes exactly as they are, so a
# checkout on a different platform never silently reflows a file and no one is
# handed a whole-file diff they did not create.
#
# NOTE what this does NOT do: it cannot stop a TOOL from converting. Reading a
# CRLF file with Python's text mode and writing it back yields LF, which git then
# reports as every line changed -- 5,491 lines for what was a 75-line edit, on
# 2026-08-31. Preventing that requires `text` (normalising stored content), which
# would reflow all 913 files once. That is a deliberate repo-wide decision and is
# deliberately NOT taken here.
#
# When editing a file programmatically, read and write in BINARY mode.
* -text
